      "title": "Too vs. Enough (Demasiado vs. Suficiente)",
      "parts": [
        { "visual": "Too = Demasiado (más de lo necesario, generalmente negativo). \nVa ANTES del adjetivo: Too expensive (Demasiado caro). Too late (Demasiado tarde).", "audio": "Too means more than necessary. It is usually negative. It goes BEFORE the adjective. For example: The project is too expensive. We are too late." },
        { "visual": "Enough = Suficiente (la cantidad necesaria). \nVa DESPUÉS del adjetivo: The office is big enough (Es lo suficientemente grande). \nVa ANTES del sustantivo: We don't have enough time (No tenemos suficiente tiempo).", "audio": "Enough means the necessary amount. It goes AFTER the adjective, for example: The office is big enough. And it goes BEFORE the noun, for example: We don't have enough time." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "stg_quiz_choice",
      "type": "quiz_choice",
